WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.762
Most agencies can show a dashboard
with millions of events a day.

2
00:00:03.762 --> 00:00:05.788
But that only measures what arrived.

3
00:00:05.788 --> 00:00:07.187
It can't show what didn't.

4
00:00:07.187 --> 00:00:11.092
Gaps stay silent in four ways: a
source that was never connected,

5
00:00:11.092 --> 00:00:15.522
a connector that looks healthy but
delivers nothing, data stored where

6
00:00:15.522 --> 00:00:19.876
no rule ever reads it, and logging
that someone switched off on purpose.

7
00:00:19.876 --> 00:00:23.598
The 2023 intrusion into
government mailboxes was caught

8
00:00:23.598 --> 00:00:26.700
by an agency that happened
to have the right logs.

9
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.950
Others had nothing to look
at, and nothing told them so.

10
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.625
So the takeaway: measure coverage
against your asset inventory,

11
00:00:33.625 --> 00:00:35.150
not against what showed up.

12
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.640
Next, the difference between
storing and detecting.
